            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note1" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" value="THE ONE IDEA&#xa;&#xa;The unit of analysis is an evidence opportunity —&#xa;one reviewed work item — never a unit of clock time.&#xa;&#xa;Repository activity is bursty, so a calendar bin gives&#xa;unequal and partly empty samples. Timestamps survive&#xa;as provenance only: never a bin, an axis, or a boundary." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="380" x="90" y="900" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note2" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" value="WHY BUNDLING IS PER PRACTICE&#xa;&#xa;The practice is part of an opportunity&#39;s KEY. PR #104 is&#xa;a different opportunity for every practice that judged it,&#xa;and none at all for a practice that stayed silent.&#xa;&#xa;Bundling globally would fill &quot;the newest four&quot; with work&#xa;items a given practice never spoke about — the bundle&#xa;would count activity instead of evidence." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="420" x="1030" y="900" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note3" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#d4e1f5;strokeColor=#3d6ea5;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" value="STANDING vs TREND&#xa;&#xa;Same opportunities, two questions, no influence either way.&#xa;A DECLINING trend never lowers a standing; a STRENGTH&#xa;standing never lifts a trend.&#xa;&#xa;Standing describes the latest work and may move with every&#xa;item. A trend asserts a CHANGE and must be evidenced —&#xa;which is why it says UNCERTAIN most of the time." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="380" x="1540" y="900" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note4" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" value="areaWeight applies ONLY at area level, and to BOTH halves:&#xa;· area standing — weighted mean of the practice shares&#xa;· area trend — weight ÷ variance, so certainty counts too&#xa;A practice is never judged more harshly for being weighted;&#xa;weight 0 withdraws its vote while it stays fully reviewed." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="420" x="560" y="940" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
